   "wikipedia_it": {
    "testo": "La fiera della vanità è un romanzo dello scrittore britannico William Makepeace Thackeray, apparso prima in venti puntate mensili tra il 1847 e il 1848, poi pubblicato come opera unica nel 1848.",
    "fonte": "https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_fiera_della_vanit%C3%A0"
   },
   "wikipedia_en": {
    "testo": "Vanity Fair is a satirical novel by the English author William Makepeace Thackeray, which follows the lives of Becky Sharp and Amelia Sedley amid their friends and families during and after the Napoleonic Wars. It was first published as a 19-volume monthly serial from 1847 to 1848, carrying the subtitle Pen and Pencil Sketches of English Society, which reflects both its satirisation of early 19th-century British society and the many illustrations drawn by Thackeray to accompany the text. It was published as a single volume in 1848 with the subtitle A Novel without a Hero. It is sometimes considered the \"principal founder\" of the Victorian domestic novel.",
    "fonte": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanity_Fair_(novel)"
   }
  },
